<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA M1 RISES 8.57 PCT, M2 UP 3.02 PCT IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA M1 RISES 8.57 PCT, M2 UP 3.02 PCT IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to</p>
<p>818.7 billion levs on June 13 from 754.1 billion levs a week</p>
<p>earlier and M2 increased to 3,632.8 billion levs from 3,526.3</p>
<p>billion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money rose 3.33 percent to 3,858.7 billion levs</p>
<p>in the week to June 13.</p>
<p>Conversion of dollar-denominated deposits into levs was</p>
<p>made at the central bank fixings of 1,677.3 levs per dollar for</p>
<p>June 13, 1660.6 for June 6 and 1,568.1 for May 30.</p>
<p> PERCENTAGE CHANGE		  JUNE 13-JUNE 6   JUNE 13-MAY 30</p>
